<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<display version="2.0.0">
  <name>BLM Rawdata</name>
  <width>1250</width>
  <height>820</height>
  <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
    <name>Title</name>
    <text>Rawdata acquisition - CH$(CH)</text>
    <x>15</x>
    <y>10</y>
    <width>400</width>
    <height>30</height>
    <font>
      <font name="Header 2" family="Liberation Sans" style="BOLD" size="18.0">
      </font>
    </font>
  </widget>
  <widget type="group" version="3.0.0">
    <name>Trigger</name>
    <x>12</x>
    <y>37</y>
    <width>588</width>
    <height>183</height>
    <font>
      <font name="Header 3" family="Liberation Sans" style="BOLD" size="16.0">
      </font>
    </font>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>Title</name>
      <text>Trigger configuration</text>
      <width>250</width>
      <height>24</height>
    </widget>
    <widget type="combo" version="2.0.0">
      <name>Mode</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):RAW:TRIG_MODE</pv_name>
      <y>30</y>
      <width>175</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(P):RAW:TRIG_MODE (RAW_TRIG_MODE)

Selects what starts a rawdata acquisition:
  Internal - the FPGA captures on its own internal timing, no external signal
             is required.
  External - the capture waits for the external trigger input.
  Self     - the capture fires when the channel selected in Self channel
             crosses Self threshold, so a single shot is taken without any
             external hardware.

Written to the FPGA immediately on selection.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
      <items>
        <item>Internal</item>
        <item>External</item>
        <item>Self</item>
      </items>
    </widget>
    <widget type="textentry" version="3.0.0">
      <name>Threshold</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):RAW:SELF_TRIG_TH</pv_name>
      <x>185</x>
      <y>30</y>
      <width>175</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
      <tooltip>$(P):RAW:SELF_TRIG_TH (RAW_SELF_TRIG_TH)

Signal level the self trigger compares against, in mV. The value is converted
back to raw ADC counts with the inverse calibration of the selected
self-trigger channel before it is written to the FPGA, so it stays valid after
recalibration, and changing the channel re-applies it. Only used when Trigger
mode is Self.

A negative level is sent as the two's-complement count, the same encoding the
ADC data itself carries; the FPGA compares that count signed, so a negative
level means what it says. The register is write-only, so to see exactly what was
sent read 'FPGA misc_ctrl.self_trigger_threshold=&lt;count&gt; (0x...) from
CH&lt;n&gt; level=&lt;mV&gt; mV' in the DEBUG log.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="combo" version="2.0.0">
      <name>Channel</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):RAW:SELF_TRIG_CH</pv_name>
      <x>370</x>
      <y>30</y>
      <width>175</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(P):RAW:SELF_TRIG_CH (RAW_SELF_TRIG_CH)

Channel 0..5 whose signal the self trigger watches, and whose calibration is
used to convert Self threshold from calibrated units back into raw ADC
counts. Only used when Trigger mode is Self.

The enum restricts the value to 0..5: the driver uses it directly as an index
into the per-channel calibration arrays, so an out-of-range value would read
past the end of those arrays.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
      <items>
        <item>CH0</item>
        <item>CH1</item>
        <item>CH2</item>
        <item>CH3</item>
        <item>CH4</item>
        <item>CH5</item>
      </items>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>ModeLabel</name>
      <text>Trigger mode</text>
      <y>64</y>
      <width>175</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>ThresholdLabel</name>
      <text>Self threshold</text>
      <x>185</x>
      <y>64</y>
      <width>175</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>ChannelLabel</name>
      <text>Self channel</text>
      <x>370</x>
      <y>64</y>
      <width>175</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
    <widget type="textentry" version="3.0.0">
      <name>Decimation</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):RAW:SAMP_DCM</pv_name>
      <y>92</y>
      <width>175</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
      <tooltip>$(P):RAW:SAMP_DCM (RAW_SAMP_DCM)

Sample decimation of the rawdata capture. Only every Nth sample is stored, so
a larger value covers a longer time span over the same 2000 point buffer at
the cost of time resolution. Minimum is 1, which keeps every sample.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="textupdate" version="2.0.0">
      <name>Count</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):RAW:TRIG_CNT</pv_name>
      <x>185</x>
      <y>92</y>
      <width>175</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
      <vertical_alignment>1</vertical_alignment>
      <tooltip>$(P):RAW:TRIG_CNT (RAW_TRIG_CNT)

Number of rawdata acquisitions completed since the IOC started, incremented by
the rawdata thread. Use it to confirm that triggers are actually arriving.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="textupdate" version="2.0.0">
      <name>Time</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):TIME_S</pv_name>
      <x>370</x>
      <y>92</y>
      <width>175</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
      <vertical_alignment>1</vertical_alignment>
      <tooltip>$(P):TIME_S (TIME_S)

Current timestamp from the selected time source, formatted as
YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.nnnnnnnnn. Switch the source between system time and
White Rabbit on the System page.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>DecimationLabel</name>
      <text>Sample decimation</text>
      <y>126</y>
      <width>175</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>CountLabel</name>
      <text>Trigger count</text>
      <x>185</x>
      <y>126</y>
      <width>175</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>TimeLabel</name>
      <text>Acquisition time</text>
      <x>370</x>
      <y>126</y>
      <width>175</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
  </widget>
